Since 2026.06.0 · Maturity Incubating · Issues PY-56267 <p>Suppresses PyCharm's missing docstring inspection for <code>@overload</code> signatures while keeping the implementation subject to the normal docstring rule.</p> BeforeResult <pre><code>from typing import overload

@overload
def parse(value: str) -&gt; int: ...

@overload
def parse(value: bytes) -&gt; int: ...

def parse(value: str | bytes) -&gt; int:
    """Parse a numeric value."""
    return int(value)
</code></pre> <pre><code># The overload signatures are not flagged for missing docstrings.
# The implementation still needs its own docstring.
</code></pre>

